# UI Patterns

## Admin modal structure
All admin modals (Customer SLA, Allowed Images, etc.) follow a two-component pattern:

- **`Toolbar<Name>Modal`** — wraps `<Modal>` + open/close state, fetches data, owns the list state
- **`<Name>AdminPanelBody`** — renders the list with edit/delete controls

## Row edit pattern (read → edit → save/cancel)
Rows display as text by default. Clicking "Edit" switches that row to inputs.

```tsx
const [editingId, setEditingId] = useState<string | null>(null)
const [editDraft, setEditDraft] = useState<MyRecord | null>(null)

// In JSX — each row:
{editingId === row.id ? (
  <>
    <input value={editDraft!.name} onChange={e => setEditDraft({...editDraft!, name: e.target.value})} />
    <button onClick={saveEdit}>Save</button>
    <button onClick={() => setEditingId(null)}>Cancel</button>
    <button onClick={() => removeRow(row.id)}>Remove</button>
  </>
) : (
  <>
    <span>{row.name}</span>
    <button onClick={() => { setEditingId(row.id); setEditDraft(row) }}>Edit</button>
  </>
)}
```

## API client (`ui/src/api.ts`)
- Every resource gets typed `Record` type + `apiList*`, `apiCreate*`, `apiUpdate*`, `apiDelete*` functions
- All functions call `apiGet<T>` / `apiPost` / `apiPut` / `apiDelete` helpers — never raw `fetch`

## Warning badges
Use the `.imageNameWarn` CSS class for inline warning badges next to field values:
```tsx
{!isValid && <span className="imageNameWarn">Unknown image</span>}
```

## About dialog
The `ComponentHealth` type includes `host?: string`. Show it next to the health dot:
```tsx
<HealthDot h={components.postgres} />
{components.postgres.host && <span className="aboutHost">{components.postgres.host}</span>}
```

## CSS naming
- Modal containers: `modalBox`, `modalOverlay`, `modalTitle`
- Admin panel body: camelCase prefixed by feature (e.g. `slaRow`, `allowedImgRow`)
- Status/badge variants: descriptive suffix (`imageNameWarn`, `aboutHost`, `aboutCommitBadge`)
